PERF FIX (post-approval, found in e2e): GET /api/lineage/roots hung ("insta locks") on a populated catalog.
- Root cause: GetEvidenceStatusCountsByFilters ran one `SELECT DISTINCT ON (uuid) * FROM evidences` (full latest-stream scan) PER filter — O(filters) full-table scans. Reproduced: 1 standard catalog / 150 controls / 150 filters / 5000 evidence = 28.95s (empty stays ~2ms).
- Fix: rewrote it as a single query per ~50-filter chunk — a MATERIALIZED `latest` CTE (DISTINCT ON runs ONCE) + UNION ALL of per-filter aggregations, with a recursive labelScopeToSQL builder mirroring getScopeClause (=, !=, AND/OR nesting). Same dataset now 414ms (~70x). Correctness asserted: all 150 controls roll up satisfied / 100%.
- Also fixed internal/tests/migrate.go: the hand-maintained TestMigrator AutoMigrate list was missing relational.ControlLink, so any lineage integration test 500'd on `relation "control_links" does not exist`. Added it (catalog_type column is picked up automatically since the list AutoMigrates relational.Catalog).
- Added internal/api/handler/lineage_perf_integration_test.go (build tag integration): reproduces the scenario, asserts correctness, and guards <5s to prevent an N+1 regression.
